<%# The pushes the bot sends on its own, each bound to one setting the jobs
    read. Nothing to fill in here: body, name, language and button label all
    follow from the kind, so the only choice left is which of them to run.

    Cards rather than table rows: what matters about a push is the wording the
    citizen receives, and a multi-line quoted message in a table cell read as a
    second row. The technical name is not repeated here — it is in the slot
    summary at the top of the page, where it is one column among five. %>
<section class="mt-5">
  <h2 class="kern-heading-medium mb-2">
    <%= t("adm.whatsapp.show.notification_templates_title") %>
  </h2>

  <p class="kern-body adm-whatsapp-page--explanation mb-3">
    <%= t("adm.whatsapp.show.notification_templates_intro",
      language: ::Whatsapp.broadcast_template_language) %>
  </p>

  <%# The voting rows are three per moment where every other push is one, so what
      picks between them is said here rather than left to be inferred from the
      row labels. %>
  <p class="kern-body adm-whatsapp-page--explanation mb-4">
    <%= t("adm.whatsapp.show.notification_templates_voting_intro") %>
  </p>

  <div class="adm-whatsapp-page--notification-cards">
    <%= render partial: "adm/whatsapp/notification_template_card",
      collection: @notification_templates, as: :notification_template %>
  </div>
</section>
